{"availability":"available","full":"NagaYu/hybrid-voice-separation","name":"hybrid-voice-separation","description":"Educational demo: hybrid air + bone conduction voice separation (synthetic-data DSP pipeline)","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-23T13:07:15Z","updated":"2026-06-29T04:21:45Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["audio-processing","bone-conduction","dsp","python","real-time","signal-processing","speech-enhancement"],"demo":"https://www.python.org/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:49:29.862Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T23:49:29.862Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T23:49:29.862Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:44:46.862Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T07:32:44.755Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T17:26:45.601Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T23:49:29.862Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A proof-of-concept demo of a hybrid DSP pipeline that dynamically fuses two microphone streams — an air-conduction mic (clear highs but heavy noise) and a bone-conduction mic (zero noise but missing highs) — to reconstruct speech in noisy environments. It implements block-wise streaming for real-time calls (ring buffer), band-wise dynamic SNR scoring, frequency-domain cross-fading, and non-linear bandwidth extension (artificial harmonic generation), all with minimal dependencies (NumPy / SciPy).","The bone-conduction signal (orange) drops off above 3 kHz, but the restored output (green) tracks the clean reference (gray dashed) and fills the band gap. The air mic (red) has that band buried in the noise floor."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NagaYu/hybrid-voice-separation/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"183e4f4c4bef117e20a896c871086dc7d19372dc1407506e415652f5068d14f4","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:47.031Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:49:29.951Z","